BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gaysian Gala 4.0
DTSTART:20260502T170000
DTEND:20260502T170000
UID:2553a7395227588656ff5c78e494ce44@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join drag diva Tanya Smania for Tranzac’s first opera reside
 ncy with OPERA QUEENS kicking off on Sat\, May 2 from 5-7 PM! Free entry -
  no tickets required\, PWYC: doors and bar open at 5 PM - show at 5:30 PM.
  This May 2026\, Opera Queens proudly brings back our 4th annual Gaysian G
 ala\, celebrating AAPI (Asian &amp\; Asian Pacific Islander) Heritage Mont
 h. Join Tanya with pianist Suzanne Yeo exploring and unpacking a wide-rang
 ing program of music by Asian composers and the complex canon of music ins
 pired by the East\, from Lehár’s “Land of Smiles”\, Delibe’s “L
 akmé”\, Alice Ping Yee Ho\, Chan Ka Nin\, and more. Tanya Smania (she/t
 hem) has been seen and heard ‘round the globe from the Canadian Opera Co
 mpany and Halifax Pride to the UK\, Europe\, the States\, and Australia. S
 ignature roles include Tchaikovsky’s Tatyana\, Bizet’s Carmen\, and Mo
 zart’s Queen of the Night. Opera Queens presents classical vocal music p
 resented in FULL COLOUR - QTBIPOC in drag\, gender-bent\, and queerified. 
 Sorry\, Timmy Chalamet - opera is awesome and we’re dragging it kicking 
 and screaming into the 21st century in the way it should be be - inclusive
 \, accessible\, and fun! Join us the first Saturdays of May to September f
 rom 5-7 PM as we welcome Toronto’s finest QTBIPOC special guests crossin
 g disciplines up close and personal - no mics and low tech\, but high camp
  and drama! Learn more at www.OperaQueens.ca and @OperaQueens. ‍
LOCATION:Tranzac Club\, 292 Brunswick Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/gaysian-gala-4-0
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Inheritance: presented by FOMO &amp\; Farrin
DTSTART:20260502T200000
DTEND:20260502T200000
UID:ab11b69d4148bd374691954c0d640b22@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Film Talk &amp\; Show Tickets – These tickets are valid for 
 programming from 8:00pm to 10:00pm. Film Talk &amp\; Show and After-Party 
 Tickets – These tickets are valid for all programming from 8:00pm until 
 2:00am. After-Party Tickets – These tickets are valid from 10:00pm onwar
 ds. After-Party Door tickets available – Cash only Join us on Saturday\,
  May 2nd for a night of art\, conversation\, music and film presented by F
 arrin and FOMO. Farrin\, is a Jamaican-queer coming-of-age film in develop
 ment\, that explores identity\, belonging\, and migration through the live
 s of two young women navigating home\, heritage\, and the future. Rooted i
 n Jamaica and shaped across the diaspora\, the film centres Caribbean voic
 es often underrepresented on screen. The evening will feature sharings fro
 m the director about the journey to bringing Farrin into production and th
 e intention behind the story\, alongside exclusive previews\, and a guided
  conversation with the audience. In between film findings\, enjoy live per
 formances and visual art from local artists. Afterward\, the space will tr
 ansform into an after-party curated by Toronto’s favourite QTBIPOC party
  FOMO\, with sounds by DJ Shannyn Hill and DJ Young Zee. ‍
LOCATION:Buddies in Bad Times\, 12 Alexander St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/inheritance-presented-by-fomo-farrin
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CFCF\, BABY BLUE (Prince Josh + Young Teesh) and Jaime Sin present
 ed by Cold Pod x Standard Time
DTSTART:20260502T210000
DTEND:20260502T210000
UID:b7688f062bcdd082e803712a133f75c7@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Cold Pod x Standard Time welcomes CFCF to Toronto alongside BA
 BY BLUE (Prince Josh + Young Teesh) and Jaime Sin for a fun one! Shapeshif
 ting LA-via-Montreal producer CFCF has amassed a diverse and thought-provo
 king catalog over the past 15 years\, moving across genres from balearic d
 isco to kitschy drum’n’bass\, and culminating in the dizzying alt-elec
 tronica opus ‘Memoryland’ in 2021. His follow-up\, ‘L.U.V.’ is due
  this June\, once again evolving his sound toward glitzy dancepop and elec
 troclash\, as evidenced on first singles “ultra-obscene!” featuring Ar
 gentinian duo EQ\, and the raucous “Let’s K*** Ourselves” featuring 
 LA-based indie-electronic band Touching Ice and Miami party-girl duo TECHG
 1RLS. ‍
LOCATION:Standard Time\, 165 Geary Avenue #2nd Floor Unit A
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/cfcf-baby-blue-prince-josh-young-teesh-and
 -jaime-sin-presented-by-cold-pod-x-standard-time
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
